# Smart Pantry & Recipe Scout Rules

## Project Goal

Build a React + TypeScript app that recommends recipes based on ingredients the user already has.

The app must support:
- ingredient text input
- fuzzy or incomplete ingredient handling
- recipe suggestions
- missing ingredient display
- food waste reduction tips
- simulated image input using sample fridge ingredients

## Tech Stack

- React
- TypeScript
- Vite
- Plain CSS
- No backend for the MVP
- Prefer local rule-based logic over external APIs for the first working version

## Code Style

- Use clear component names.
- Keep components small.
- Put reusable logic in `src/services`.
- Put static sample recipe data in `src/data`.
- Avoid overengineering.
- Do not add authentication, databases, or deployment unless explicitly requested.

## AI Usage Expectations

When generating code:
- Explain what files were changed.
- Keep changes focused on the current feature branch.
- Avoid rewriting unrelated files.
- Include simple edge case handling.
- Prefer readable code over clever code.

## Testing Expectations

After changes:
- Make sure `npm run dev` works.
- Make sure `npm run build` works before final submission.
- Manually test at least these inputs:
  - eggs, rice, spinach
  - old spinach, leftover rice, eggg
  - tomatos, pasta, cheese
  - milk, bread, banana
  - empty input

## Documentation

Maintain:
- `README.md`
- `docs/PROJECT_REPORT.md`
- `docs/AI_USAGE_REPORT.md`